WEBVTT

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:07.050
Osaka's captain, Hirata, intercepts again!

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:13.140
Hauer, Katayama, Hatake, Kubota.

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:15.890
The four forwards are gunning for the goal.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:19.890
This is Osaka Gunner's ultra attacking line-up they pride themselves in!

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:24.020
Here, here!

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:25.770
Hurry up and pass it here!

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:27.950
Uh...

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:33.570
Got it!

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:37.870
Clear it, clear it!

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.120
Uhh...

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:44.000
Kubo, here!

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:02.690
GOAL!

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:05.910
Hatake scores to put Osaka 4 up!

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:08.440
And it's only been 40 minutes!

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:12.240
Osaka's relentless assault has given Kofu a huge mountain to climb.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:14.550
"Might be"?

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.120
Are you confident?

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:23.870
Of course I am. Aren't you, Murakoshi?

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:28.750
What kind of player goes out on the field expecting to lose?

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:33.930
Isn't that right? Let's just sweep Osaka aside.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:41.390
Plus, I'm interested in how ETU will handle them.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:47.400
ETU? There's no one from there that's representing the nation, right?

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:50.010
I'm looking forward to it.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:57.260
What kind of football will you show me, Monsieur Tatsumi?

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:46.690
Right, and that is all. Did everybody get it?

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:48.750
Any questions?

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:51.500
What? That's all?

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.760
Is this guy for real?

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:15.470
Huh? No comments?

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:22.630
Bravo! I think it's fabulous, Tatsumi.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:24.490
You sound sarcastic.

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:25.860
Uhh, to be honest...

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:28.650
Your plan sounds kinda fun,

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:31.120
but will things be that smooth-sailing?

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:34.540
Osaka won by 8 goals yesterday,

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.920
while we were defeated in our previous game.

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:43.960
What's the matter, Kuro? Are you lacking confidence?

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.180
No, I have plenty!

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:50.770
Whether the plan succeeds or not is all up to you.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:57.810
I came up with this plan because I believe it will work.

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:04.320
Though Osaka have four forwards,

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:07.980
we have four defenders.

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:10.080
They don't have a numerical advantage.

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:16.960
I feel that the difference in quality is the main problem rather than quantity.

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:18.710
Akasaki!

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:24.170
Kuro identified the key to this just now; which is that my plan is fun.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.500
That's the important part.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:30.380
The question is whether or not you can enjoy yourselves in this game.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:33.730
If you carry out my instructions, this game...

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:36.980
will be one hell of a ride.

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:41.580
If there were to be a thrilling match, the fans will get excited well.

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:45.150
This will allow you to enjoy yourselves even more.

00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:53.000
That's the time when you can play better than you've ever imagined.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:56.700
And as a result,

00:05:56.700 --> 00:06:00.270
we will be the first to clean up the undefeated Osaka team.

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:03.880
See, doesn't that sound fun?

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:12.760
Alright, ready?

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:17.940
Well, in order to do that, you will have to drill whatever I will be telling you into your heads.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:19.020
Let's start!

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:21.020
Ok!

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:24.900
Alright, let's destroy Osaka!

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.520
Don't forget your roles!

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:27.530
Let's do it.

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:34.860
Baki, you'll just have to keep chasing after the ball as always.

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:35.660
Understood.

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:01.690
Thank you.

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:02.930
Wow, it's pizza!

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:28.770
The forwards: Katayama, followed by Hatake.

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:30.340
The defender: Biva.

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:35.470
I guess being undefeated brings confidence as they're all looking strong.

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:42.850
The Japanese internationals: Shimura, Hiraga, and Terauchi.

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:48.740
And the young wonderkid, Komuro, who's both a national and Olympic player.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:54.620
Though they're all defenders, Osaka still have four national players.

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:59.010
And ETU doesn't even have one...

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:01.370
In addition,

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:07.250
they have the league's top scorer.

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:13.750
Hauer, the Dutchman. With him around, their offense is devastating.

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:31.070
Osaka Gunner's latest addition among the 4 forwards: Kubota.

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:39.230
Since Dulfer became their manager, he's been a first team regular.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:42.790
When they shoot, it's awesome!

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:44.190
It's so intense!

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:48.390
Alright, I'm pumped up for this!

00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:50.300
Let's beat Osaka!

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:54.290
ETU! ETU! East Tokyo United!

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:58.180
Hey, join me! It's embarrassing to do it alone!

00:08:58.180 --> 00:08:59.710
But Kota...

00:08:59.710 --> 00:09:01.720
today's match is a difficult one.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:06.390
Osaka have four national players,

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:10.480
and they have 4 forwards in their ultra attacking line-up.

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:15.610
Do you really think ETU's defense can shut them down?

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:20.120
That's true...

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:21.250
See?

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:34.260
Tetta, Yoshio! Look!

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:38.760
It's the national coach, Blanc!

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:41.180
Blanc, Blanc!

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:42.590
Blanc?

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:44.020
Seriously?

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:50.150
Those cute kids are running this way. Should I give them my autograph?

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:51.900
N-no, you can't!

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:55.110
We're in a hurry and it'll cause a ruckus here!

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:57.320
Aww, they'll have a bad impression of me!

00:09:57.610 --> 00:10:02.160
It'll be okay, please do it another time.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:04.260
Blanc is going away.

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:05.290
Wait...

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:09.920
I'm sorry, kids. It's this evil guy's fault.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:14.410
Hey Blanc! Stop using our players!

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:16.890
It'll hinder the team's performances!

00:10:16.890 --> 00:10:18.740
You're in trouble if they get injured!

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:20.550
Are you listening, Blanc?!

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.330
Scary...

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:26.310
But I'm kinda jealous that they can say something like that.

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:30.540
Hey, since Blanc is watching today...

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:31.590
Yeah?

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:34.690
If our players perform well today...

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:39.530
That means...

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:45.200
ETU will have a national player?!

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:48.270
Hey, I'm all fired up!

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:50.720
Let's cheer our hearts out!

00:10:50.720 --> 00:10:52.560
Let's beat Osaka!

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:55.450
That might be hard to achieve, but do your best, ETU!

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:56.700
Yeah!

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:03.600
Yes, the candidates will be announced after the game, as usual.

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:06.370
Hey, have you seen my coat?

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:08.220
Nope.

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:11.850
That's weird, where did I put it?

00:11:21.470 --> 00:11:26.330
Where would you prefer to watch the match from?

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:39.990
Haven't see you in a while, Takeshi Tatsumi.

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:42.890
Hello, Dulfer.

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:47.750
What're you doing, Monsieur Blanc?

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:55.040
The two managers are exchanging sparks.

00:11:55.040 --> 00:12:01.530
It might look like a friendly conversation, but they are trying to read each other.

00:12:03.170 --> 00:12:08.160
So who'll take the initiative? The battle has already begun.

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:17.480
So, Tatsumi, how confident are you about today's match?

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:23.890
Well, let's just say I'm usually not one to lack confidence.

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:34.660
Oh, I see. I guess he doesn't want to elaborate on that.

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:39.740
I can read that as a lack of confidence on his part.

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:43.450
Then, do you mind if I ask a question?

00:12:45.150 --> 00:12:48.580
Dulfer, you're Dutch, right?

00:12:51.510 --> 00:12:53.080
Is it true that in Holland...

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:57.610
there are more bikes than people?

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:08.440
What a random question. It seems that he's not under any pressure.

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:16.390
And the atmosphere's supposed to be tense right before the match... What on earth is he thinking of?

00:13:18.590 --> 00:13:20.440
What did he say?

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:23.860
Something that's not worth translating.

00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:33.120
Well, the game is about to start, so let's get a move-on.

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:35.710
I guess so.

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:51.640
Let's both do our best.

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:10.660
Alright, make sure to stretch properly.

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:14.180
The temperature's gonna drop at night. Do it right to avoid injuries.

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:19.670
Alright! I have a premonition that it's going to be a Katayama day today.

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:25.180
So Shimu, please pass the ball to me, and I'll smash it against the back of the net.

00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:26.800
Hey, Kata!

00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:31.180
You've scored three goals so far, while I've scored <i>four</i>.

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:34.060
My abilities are <i>obviously</i> better!

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:36.470
You understand right, Shimu?

00:14:36.470 --> 00:14:39.190
If you pass the ball to me, you'll get to increase your assists tally.

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:41.060
What are you babbling about?

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:44.940
Have you forgotten about the time I assisted you?

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:48.610
Hey, you're so cheap.

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:52.120
Relax, there's no need to quarrel.

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:56.700
Don't worry, I understand that both of you are doing your best in helping me to...

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:59.460
express <i>my</i> abilities.

00:15:01.320 --> 00:15:03.670
Nobody said anything like that!

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:06.590
Shimu never gets what anyone is saying.

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:08.970
Yo, Hauer!

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:13.110
Make sure to head the ball towards me, okay?

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:18.520
What? You're worrying about your hair again?!

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:22.430
Didn't we mention that it looks crap on you and your big face?

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:29.760
Crap, I think he understood what we were saying!

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:33.840
I'm sorry, Hauer! I was just kidding, so please pass the ball to me.

00:15:33.840 --> 00:15:37.630
Our Kansai forwards are being loud again.

00:15:37.630 --> 00:15:40.720
Those guys are always like that.

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:43.000
On the other hand...

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:46.770
You're quiet as always, Kubota.

00:15:50.210 --> 00:15:52.760
Oh, probably, yeah.

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:55.640
How boring!

00:15:56.680 --> 00:16:00.570
You should say something more interesting.

00:16:00.570 --> 00:16:04.400
Oh, probably, yes.

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:10.070
Are you guys done with your warm-ups?

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:14.320
You guys ready for battle?

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:17.910
We've come to this stadium to win.

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:25.580
Oh, there you are, Tatsumi. I found your jacket.

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:30.630
Where you've been? We're running out of time!

00:16:32.270 --> 00:16:33.880
I had a little chat with Dulfer.

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:37.680
Man, he looks so confident.

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:41.460
Well, that's to be expected when you're in first place and also undefeated.

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:44.230
But it went well. I'm kinda relieved.

00:16:46.170 --> 00:16:51.490
It seems he'll be using his usual ultra attacking line-up.

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:59.240
ETU is a team that bases their tactics on their opponent's playing style.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:04.670
However, we will stick to our beautiful, offensive style...

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:08.500
and overwhelm ETU.

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:12.510
ETU is a team that bases their tactics on their opponent's playing style.

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:16.020
However, we will stick to our beautiful, offensive style and overwhelm ETU.

00:17:16.020 --> 00:17:18.530
Beautiful and effective football.

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:19.050
However, we will stick to our beautiful, offensive style and overwhelm ETU.

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:22.520
We are a team that takes pride in our own playing style.

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:26.790
No matter how much they try to improvise in order to win,

00:17:27.970 --> 00:17:30.720
we will not change our principles.

00:17:32.180 --> 00:17:35.720
The Osaka Gunners' line-up is as follows...

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:55.420
Now, it's finally time.

00:17:57.320 --> 00:18:01.930
We will now announce the starting line-up of East Tokyo United.

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:06.810
Number 1, goalkeeper: Midorikawa Hiroshi!

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:09.560
Dori! Dori!

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:15.440
Number 2, defender: Kuroda Kazuki!

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:19.370
Kuroda! Kuroda!

00:18:20.510 --> 00:18:24.200
Number 3, defender: Sugie Yusaku!

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:26.680
Sugie! Sugie!

00:18:28.150 --> 00:18:32.050
Number 16, defender: Kiyokawa Kazumi!

00:18:32.050 --> 00:18:34.690
Kiyokawa! Kiyokawa!

00:18:36.620 --> 00:18:38.720
Number 22, defender...

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:41.600
Their defensive line-up is the same as always.

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:45.680
I know they have some sort of plan...

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:51.730
Number 6, midfielder: Murakoshi Shigeyuki!

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:53.810
Alright!

00:18:53.810 --> 00:18:55.860
We're counting on you, Mr. ETU!

00:18:57.220 --> 00:19:01.580
Number 7, midfielder: Tsubaki Daisuke!

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:03.910
Tsubaki! Tsubaki!

00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:09.500
Number 10, midfielder: Luigi Yoshida!

00:19:10.610 --> 00:19:11.920
Prince!
Gino!

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:17.120
Number 15, midfielder: Akasaki Ryo!

00:19:17.120 --> 00:19:19.740
Akasaki! Akasaki!

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:25.510
Number 20, forward: Sera Kyohei!

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:26.920
Sera! Sera!

00:19:26.920 --> 00:19:28.040
It's Sera.

00:19:28.040 --> 00:19:30.480
Huh? What about Tanba?

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:34.400
Number 11, forward: Natsuki Yotaro!

00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:37.280
What? Two forwards?!

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:39.410
T-Tatsumi,

00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:44.160
are you really gonna go head-to-head offensively against Osaka?!

00:19:46.230 --> 00:19:49.380
So that's your plan, Monsieur Tatsumi.

00:19:49.810 --> 00:19:52.960
And the manager: Tatsumi Takeshi!

00:19:56.110 --> 00:20:01.240
Is this the reason why ETU's practices were not open to the public lately?

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:05.480
Can this line-up do something against Osaka's devastating offense?

00:20:53.030 --> 00:20:56.980
They have firm expressions. The both of them.

00:20:58.350 --> 00:21:03.460
This match might prove to be quite interesting.

00:21:05.310 --> 00:21:07.990
Alright, let's keep our voices up for the match!

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:12.120
Focus! If you let your guard down, they'll send us to the cleaners!

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:16.480
Side-backs, stick close to Katayama and Hatake.

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:17.750
Yes!

00:21:18.670 --> 00:21:22.630
Oh my, the defense is all pumped up.

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:26.960
Then I too, shall do my best just for today.

00:21:26.960 --> 00:21:29.390
What's that "just for today" supposed to mean?

00:21:31.820 --> 00:21:34.190
Alright, I'm calm.

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:42.780
I'll show you! I'll show you! I'll show you!

00:21:43.830 --> 00:21:47.950
Sera's fired up, but he looks kinda scary.

00:21:53.980 --> 00:21:58.040
On the other hand, Natsu looks nervous.

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:01.550
Listen up, we did everything we could.

00:22:02.030 --> 00:22:04.490
Now we just have to show it on the pitch!

00:22:06.280 --> 00:22:08.720
We'll defeat Osaka. Let's go!

00:22:08.990 --> 00:22:09.800
Yeah!

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:17.020
Very good, that's the spirit. Don't let them outrun you!

00:22:18.740 --> 00:22:19.920
Just you watch.

00:22:23.740 --> 00:22:29.820
I'm going to snap your stuck-up nose in the next 90 minutes, Dulfer.

00:24:15.600 --> 00:24:18.180
It's only a 20cm difference.

00:24:18.390 --> 00:24:19.660
Katayama is coming!

00:24:19.660 --> 00:24:21.690
Stop me if you can.

00:24:21.690 --> 00:24:25.120
Teams on a winning streak do look different.

00:24:25.120 --> 00:24:28.480
They're picking up where they left off during the last game.
